          ],
          "content": "Ganita Manjari | Grade 9 | Part I"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.131,
            0.115,
            0.399,
            0.138
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Think and Reflect"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.158,
            0.152,
            0.734,
            0.195
          ],
          "content": "1. Try to evaluate the following using a suitable identity: (i) $3 5 ^ { 2 }$ (ii) $6 5 ^ { 2 }$ (iii) $8 5 ^ { 2 }$ (iv) $1 0 5 ^ { 2 }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.178,
            0.199,
            0.573,
            0.218
          ],
          "content": "Do you observe any interesting pattern?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.158,
            0.221,
            0.854,
            0.26
          ],
          "content": "2. Observe the two rows of figures below. They represent an algebraic identity. Try to identify it."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.125,
            0.272,
            0.871,
            0.675
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_10_image_6.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.712,
            0.662,
            0.736
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "4.5 Factorisation Using Algebra Tiles"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.746,
            0.68,
            0.767
          ],
          "content": "Consider a rectangle with sides $x + 3$ and $x + 4$ units."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.771,
            0.875,
            0.818
          ],
          "content": "We know that the area of such a rectangle is $\\left(x+3\\right)\\left(x+4\\right)$ sq. units. Using distributivity, we get"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.277,
            0.822,
            0.758,
            0.842
          ],
          "content": "(x + 3)(x + 4) = x^{2} + 3x + 4x + 12 = x^{2} + 7x + 12.",
          "image_source": "images/page_10_equation_10.jpg"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
